WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.379 --> 00:00:02.595
- My mom thought I was
crazy when I told her I was

00:00:02.595 --> 00:00:05.592
into underwater hockey,
and she continues to think

00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:09.140
I'm crazy when I show up with black eyes.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.380
But she's also my biggest
fan when I'm at the

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.784
World Championships.

00:00:12.784 --> 00:00:15.284
(jazzy music)

00:00:17.792 --> 00:00:20.174
My name is Tyera Eulberg,
and I'm the Captain of

00:00:20.174 --> 00:00:22.873
the U.S. Women's Underwater Hockey Team.

00:00:22.873 --> 00:00:25.570
So underwater hockey is played six-on-six.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:30.043
We're not wearing tanks, just
fins and a mask and snorkel.

00:00:30.043 --> 00:00:32.811
The puck is weighted and sits
on the bottom of the pool,

00:00:32.811 --> 00:00:36.662
and players use a short
one-handed stick to play the puck.

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:40.043
Unlike ice hockey there is no
goalie in underwater hockey,

00:00:40.043 --> 00:00:42.731
and the snorkel helps you
watch the play while you're

00:00:42.731 --> 00:00:45.302
recovering on the surface,
but otherwise you're holding

00:00:45.302 --> 00:00:48.593
your breath when you're
actually involved in the play.

00:00:48.593 --> 00:00:50.873
(jazzy music)

00:00:50.873 --> 00:00:53.193
We take underwater hockey very seriously.

00:00:53.193 --> 00:00:55.731
The U.S. Women's National
Team compete at the

00:00:55.731 --> 00:00:56.963
World Championships.

00:00:56.963 --> 00:00:59.953
They're held every two
years, and they bring in

00:00:59.953 --> 00:01:02.723
about 25 different countries
to compete to be the

00:01:02.723 --> 00:01:04.140
best of the best.

00:01:06.113 --> 00:01:09.993
It really is the ultimate
team sport because there's no

00:01:09.993 --> 00:01:13.660
puck hog that can just do
everything for your team.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:15.553
Eventually that person's
going to have to come up

00:01:15.553 --> 00:01:18.393
to breathe, and you have
to have a teammate there

00:01:18.393 --> 00:01:20.119
to take your place.

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:22.502
If I'm about to score, and
I'm running out of air,

00:01:22.502 --> 00:01:24.585
I'm gonna freakin' score.

00:01:26.451 --> 00:01:29.039
We see people coming to
underwater hockey both from

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:32.971
swimming backgrounds and
from ice hockey backgrounds.

00:01:32.971 --> 00:01:36.331
We struggle from the fact
that most people in the

00:01:36.331 --> 00:01:39.391
United States don't grow up playing it.

00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:42.361
People don't grow up holding
their breath and trying to

00:01:42.361 --> 00:01:44.113
kick hard underwater.

00:01:44.113 --> 00:01:47.152
They grow up playing soccer
and playing basketball.

00:01:47.152 --> 00:01:50.840
There's no money in underwater
hockey, so we're absolutely

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.142
doing it for the love of the sport.

00:01:54.142 --> 00:01:55.491
I love underwater hockey.

00:01:55.491 --> 00:01:56.824
It's so elegant.

00:01:57.702 --> 00:02:00.981
Being underwater is
just a beautiful thing.

00:02:00.981 --> 00:02:02.891
I feel like some really
gorgeous sea creature

00:02:02.891 --> 00:02:04.350
when I'm playing.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.933
(jazzy music)

